WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.880
There are some people who would get tired
of being placed in charge of SCP-914, or The

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:05.880
Clockworks.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.490
The monotony of it all might make most of
us go mad.

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:14.570
The same routine, day after day, placing an
infinite number of objects into the Intake

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:19.539
Booth of the machine,
selecting one of the modes, be it Rough, Coarse,

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:24.050
1:1, Fine, or Very Fine,
and seeing just what sort of transformation

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.500
takes place.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.350
But there was one employee of the SCP Foundation
who liked that routine just fine.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:36.370
Dr. Gears was happy with his position, the
simplicity of the routine, the predictability

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.370
of it all.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:42.550
He liked when the days stacked neatly together
in a row of uneventful stretches of time.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:47.930
It was why he ate the exact same meal for
lunch every day: a plain turkey sandwich on

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:51.770
white bread, a cup of water, and a single
banana.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:56.350
Of course, there was some variety in the events
that came about when testing the Clockworks.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:01.250
There was that incident with Dr. Curtis, and
the pound of bacon placed inside the machine

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.570
alongside a photograph of SCP-682.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:10.880
It had resulted in a miniature replica of
SCP-682, made entirely out of bacon, capable

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.229
of movement, and extremely hostile.

00:01:14.229 --> 00:01:18.409
Though its size prevented it from doing any
damage, it did still attempt to kill any staff

00:01:18.409 --> 00:01:19.709
it could find.

00:01:19.709 --> 00:01:24.380
It had smelled mouthwatering,
but Dr. Gears had suspended Dr. Curtis from

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:29.759
testing with SCP-914 for the trouble,
and a day of having bacon grease cleaned off

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:31.740
of every surface in the vicinity.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:36.390
There was also the incident that occured when
Dr. Hertz, in an attempt to score some free

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:40.689
music production,
placed a CD of his own original guitar songs

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:43.799
into the machine on the setting "Very Fine."

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:48.289
Rather than improving the production quality
of the tracks on the CD, the machine produced

00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:53.009
a completely silent CD,
as well as a collection of books on songwriting,

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:55.810
singing, and playing the guitar for beginners.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:00.819
Dr. Gears had to physically drag Dr. Hertz
from the room when, upset by the blow to his

00:02:00.819 --> 00:02:04.009
ego, he attempted to attack the machine.

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:09.780
And of course, there had been the highly destructive
"Super Bouncy Ball" incident, which resulted

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.620
in 45 casualties and staggering damage to
the facility, as well as the aforementioned

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.290
ball
which was currently thought to be somewhere

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:20.519
in space, most likely orbiting Mars.

00:02:20.519 --> 00:02:23.680
But for the most part, it was always the same
thing:

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:29.519
an object went in, a setting was selected,
and the object came out in a new, modified

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:30.519
state.

00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:34.819
Wash, rinse, repeat, just like it said on
the back of the bottle of the brand of unscented

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:38.879
shampoo Dr. Gears had been using for the past
thirty years.

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:42.540
That was how he liked it, and as he sat at
his desk,

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.560
going over the test logs and preparing to
supervise another round of tests,

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.690
he turned on some of his favorite tunes.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.129
Well, I say tunes, but it was really a white
noise machine.

00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:56.629
He didn't care for music, it was a bit too
much excitement.

00:02:56.629 --> 00:03:01.560
He was just getting into the flow of his work,
when there was a knock at his office door.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.719
"Excuse me, sir?"

00:03:03.719 --> 00:03:09.109
A Research Assistant was standing at the door,
pale and anxious, a clipboard in his hands.

00:03:09.109 --> 00:03:11.909
"They're requesting your help with an emergency
down the hall."

00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:13.099
"What is it?"

00:03:13.099 --> 00:03:14.290
Dr. Gears asked.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.459
"They didn't really say, just something about
Dr. Bright and chainsaws?"

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:20.739
The assistant stammered.

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:23.220
Dr. Gears sighed and stood up from his desk.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.999
"I'll be right there."

00:03:24.999 --> 00:03:30.349
There wouldn't be anyone keeping an eye on
SCP-914, but at this point, the experimentation

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:32.639
process basically ran itself.

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:36.470
Everything would be fine if Dr. Gears stepped
away for a little while...wouldn't it?

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:43.140
Meanwhile, across the Site, a very enterprising
mask became keenly aware of an opportunity

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.890
presenting itself.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:49.709
It had been lying in wait, meticulously planning
and plotting for days,

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:53.739
and now, there was an opening it could take
advantage of.

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:59.389
You see, months ago, the mask had managed
to finagle itself a host, a researcher who

00:03:59.389 --> 00:04:01.609
had just been working with SCP-914.

00:04:01.609 --> 00:04:05.579
When the Mask's consciousness took over the
man's, and it got an up close and personal

00:04:05.579 --> 00:04:08.700
look at all of his thoughts as they snuffed
out one by one,

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:12.889
it learned all about the marvelous, miraculous
Clockworks.

00:04:12.889 --> 00:04:18.340
The machine capable of transforming anything
into a better version of itself.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:25.630
The Mask had fantasized, obsessed about getting
to SCP-914, of using it to mold itself, to

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:28.949
change into something greater and more powerful.

00:04:28.949 --> 00:04:35.180
Then, perhaps, it could escape this place
and return to its former freedom and glory.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:38.669
Of course, it would have to select the correct
setting.

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:42.770
One wrong choice, and the whole plan could
amount to nothing.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:48.160
On Rough, the Mask would likely be destroyed,
reduced to a pile of ceramic dust or perhaps

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.940
even a ball of unmolded clay
alongside some of the black slime always oozing

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.750
from its eyes and mouth.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:59.660
On Coarse, it would likely be transformed
into a slab of plan porcelain, uncarved and

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:00.800
unpainted.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.690
On 1:1, the Mask would likely be swapped out
with another anomalous object, some other

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:10.050
enterprising mask
or perhaps a haunted Victorian doll or some

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.259
other malicious inanimate thing.

00:05:12.259 --> 00:05:14.080
And what use would that be?

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.669
No, that wouldn't do at all.

00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:21.270
Fine could be promising, and would likely
prevent the Mask from degrading any future

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:24.840
hosts it decided to take...but why stop there?

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:31.000
Why should it limit itself to simply Fine,
when Very Fine was right there and looking

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.110
oh so promising?

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:38.940
It decided, if it could get to SCP-914, it
would find a way to transform itself using

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.990
the Very Fine setting.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:49.220
And then, its enemies, this pathetic Foundation,
the entire world...would fall to their knees.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:54.639
It had been watching patiently, like a snake
coiled and ready to snap up its prey, spreading

00:05:54.639 --> 00:05:57.699
its psychic tendrils as far as they could
go,

00:05:57.699 --> 00:06:02.860
and anticipating the moment that someone left
SCP-914 unattended.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.710
Now, the moment had arrived.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.419
Of course, the Mask would need help.

00:06:08.419 --> 00:06:11.199
It didn't have a way to reach the Clockworks
on its own.

00:06:11.199 --> 00:06:16.389
So, it had been wrapping its influence around
the guard stationed just outside its door,

00:06:16.389 --> 00:06:22.460
dripping thoughts into his head, whispering
darkness into his ear at every chance it got.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:27.530
Chipping away at his will, bit by bit, until
the man was little more than a puppet with

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:30.840
the Possessive Mask tugging at his strings.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:37.180
The Mask gave a mental yank on one of those
strings, calling the man in its thrall into

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.710
the room.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:41.580
He knocked out his fellow guard with the butt
of his gun, first.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:47.009
At this point, his mind was so pliable that
he would do anything to please the Mask.

00:06:47.009 --> 00:06:51.830
Next, the man entered the containment chamber,
a glassy, vacant look in his eyes.

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:57.419
He unlocked the glass case and reached inside,
lifting the mask out, and bringing it one

00:06:57.419 --> 00:07:00.360
step closer to absolute freedom.

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:05.850
He tucked the mask inside of his uniform,
hiding it from any prying eyes, and began

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:10.330
to walk steadily toward SCP-914's room.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:15.479
All the while, the Mask whispered silent encouragements
into the man's weakened mind, promising him

00:07:15.479 --> 00:07:22.129
power and success beyond his wildest dreams,
if only he would help it achieve this goal.

00:07:22.129 --> 00:07:26.849
Of course, the mask was planning to kill the
man as soon as his task was done, but he didn't

00:07:26.849 --> 00:07:28.659
need to know that yet.

00:07:28.659 --> 00:07:33.259
Every step brought the Mask closer to victory,
and it was practically vibrating with the

00:07:33.259 --> 00:07:36.389
delicious anticipation of it all.

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:38.250
Soon, so soon.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:42.539
They reached the containment room, the Clockworks
just beyond the door.

00:07:42.539 --> 00:07:47.719
The guard carried the Mask into the room,
placed the Mask inside of the Intake Booth,

00:07:47.719 --> 00:07:49.970
closed it, and approached the Control Panel.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:56.449
In accordance with the Mask's psychic instructions,
he selected "Very Fine," and turned the machine

00:07:56.449 --> 00:07:57.849
on.

00:07:57.849 --> 00:08:03.560
The cogs and gears inside whirred to life,
the engine sputtered, metal clanked and pipes

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:06.639
exhaled hissing bursts of energy.

00:08:06.639 --> 00:08:13.169
The Output chamber opened, and through the
curtain of steam, SCP-035 stepped in its new

00:08:13.169 --> 00:08:15.590
and improved form.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.039
That's right, stepped.

00:08:18.039 --> 00:08:24.720
First one long, sinewy leg, leathery, shiny,
and black as the night, extended into view.Another

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:31.810
leg followed, and along with it came a torso,
a pair of arms, a slender neck, and the familiar

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:36.930
face of the Mask, stark white against the
darkness of its new body.

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:41.580
The feet ended in little points, as if the
figure was wearing boots, but there was no

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.280
visible clothing.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:49.780
It was all one thing, angular and strange,
with long, long fingers tipped with curved

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:51.050
claws.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:58.870
The mask let out a wicked cackle, throwing
back its head in triumph.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:04.370
"Excellent..it's even better than I imagined."

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:07.050
The Mask turned to the guard that had helped
it escape.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:09.170
"Thank you for your service.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:13.400
Now, I have one last favor to ask you..."

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:18.200
It was time for the Mask to test its powers,
to see how the Clockworks had strengthened

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.880
what was already there.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:23.970
What more was it capable of, in this enhanced
state.

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:30.700
"I want you to go to the cafeteria, walk into
the kitchen, and climb into the oven, would

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:31.700
you?

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:34.260
Make sure you turn it on nice and hot first."

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:39.480
It waited for a few seconds, before the man
nodded solemnly, turned, and left the room,

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.820
heading off in the direction of the cafeteria.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:48.090
It listened as the moments passed, and the
sound of horrified, shocked screams rang out,

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:51.520
and it knew that the man had followed its
instructions exactly.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:56.190
At the Mask's orders, he had cooked himself
for lunch.

00:09:56.190 --> 00:10:00.030
The Mask clapped its hands together, cackling
again.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.450
"Wonderful!

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.290
Oh, wonderful.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.950
Now that's taken care of...what shall I try
next?"

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:14.260
If the Mask had eyebrows, they would have
been arched in a truly devilish expression.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:19.370
First, it wanted to test its abilities on
a truly formidable opponent, someone worthy

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:21.920
of the Mask's time and attention.

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:26.840
Casually as you please, it strode over to
one particular containment chamber, to see

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:29.540
about an unkillable reptile.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:33.740
As it walked, several guards took notice,
pointing their weapons at the Mask and ordering

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.070
it to stand down.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:39.690
Each time, it chuckled, and with a wave of
its hand, the barrels of their guns warped

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:44.070
and twisted into little metal bows, completely
useless.

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:48.600
It snapped its clawed fingers, and the guards
fell to the ground in an unconscious heap.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:54.420
"Can't have you sounding the alarm yet, the
fun is only just beginning!"

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:58.130
The Mask remarked, though it knew the guards
couldn't hear it.

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:03.250
It kicked open the door to SCP-682's containment
room with a jaunty greeting.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:06.070
"Hello, you scaly fool!

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:09.240
I've come to pay you a visit!"

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:14.480
The reptile did not respond, incapacitated
by its hydrochloric acid bath.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.230
That just wouldn't do.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:21.770
The Mask concentrated, and the steel chamber
broke apart, acid spilling everywhere, hissing

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:25.080
as it splashed onto any available surface.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:31.050
SCP-682 lifted its head, twitching its tail,
and took in the sight of the new and improved

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:32.050
Mask.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:33.570
"What do you think?"

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:35.551
The Mask posed for the creature, laughing
again.

00:11:35.551 --> 00:11:41.920
It seemed it couldn't stop laughing lately,
its expression fixed into a permanent gleeful

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:42.920
smile.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:46.870
It couldn't help it, freedom and power just
felt so good.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:48.250
"Disssgussssting."

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:52.960
SCP-682 remarked, unimpressed with this display.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:58.360
It lunged at the Mask, preparing to attack,
but the Mask held up a hand to stop it.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.910
"Not so fast."

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:07.530
SCP-682 suddenly froze in place, eyes rolling
wildly as it tried desperately, in vain, to

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:08.530
move.

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:11.990
"Let's see, what should I do with you..."

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:15.610
The Mask was itching to test out its reality-warping
abilities.

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:19.980
It had the feeling that there was very little
it couldn't do in this state, and wanted to

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:23.070
see just how far its power could go.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:27.640
But what would be suitable punishment, what
could be the cruelest possible thing to do

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.260
to such a creature?

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:34.750
The Mask could simply try to kill it, to finally
snuff out the endless, miserable life…

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:37.120
but that would be a release.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.350
That would be far too easy.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:40.350
Aha!

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:43.440
A lightbulb went off in the Mask's twisted
mind.

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:44.440
"Perfect."

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:49.380
It waved its hand, releasing SCP-682 from
its paralysis,

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:54.180
but as the massive lizard snapped its jaws
and moved to take a bite out of the Mask,

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:57.450
it lost its balance, falling to the ground.

00:12:57.450 --> 00:13:02.170
Its legs had begun to shrink, rapidly, knocking
its center of gravity askew.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:07.850
Soon, the rest of its body began to follow,
getting smaller and smaller at an unbelievable

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:10.740
pace,
until finally, where there had once stood

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:16.800
a massive, impossible, prehistoric beast,
was something resembling a baby alligator.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:22.320
A little tiny tail, thrashing about, short
stubby legs, bulbous eyes, and a mouth full

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:25.520
of sharp, but adorable non-threatening, teeth.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:32.560
When the shrunken SCP-682 spoke, its voice
was high-pitched and squeaky.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:33.560
"Disgussssting!"

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:35.160
It roared.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.160
"Yes.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.410
You are."

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:42.600
The Mask turned and left, thoroughly pleased
with its work, and shut the door behind it.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:48.130
Now, what other fellow anomalies could the
Mask exercise its absolute superiority over?

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:52.830
It pondered other supposedly "dangerous" and
"deadly" entities that it had heard about

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:55.490
over its time in Foundation custody.

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:58.000
It all seemed so...laughable now.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:04.190
There was only one true danger within these
walls, and it was the Mask.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.660
Oh, what about that abominable sculpture?

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:12.500
The ugly thing with a penchant for snapping
necks, but only when a person wasn't looking

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.500
at it.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:15.660
The absolute coward.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:23.790
Cowards didn't deserve to live, the Mask decided,
and it made its way over toward SCP-173's

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:24.790
containment room.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:29.790
Inside, there were several D-Class staring
at the statue with wide, unblinking eyes,

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:34.250
each person terrified of being the one to
let their guard down and lose their life in

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:35.680
the process.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.440
\
None of them would die today, however.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:41.800
At least...not at the hands of the statue.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:47.760
As the D-Class in the cell watched, never
once taking their eyes off of SCP-173, the

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:52.690
statue's head began to twist and rotate, the
sound of cracking snow and creaking metal

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:54.860
reverberating through the room.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:15:00.170
The Mask used its telekinetic abilities to
rend the statue's head from its neck, relishing

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:05.910
the irony of breaking the thing's neck just
as it had done to so many others.

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:12.320
It wasn't about justice, of course, the Mask
had no taste for such insipid and human things,

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.750
it just found the whole image quite funny.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:20.290
the entire thing began to crumble apart
like a sandcastle beneath an ocean wave,

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:24.790
disintegrating until all that was left was
a pile of pebbles and dust.

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:29.800
Just like that, SCP-173 was no more.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:34.910
As for the D-Class in the cell, well, the
Mask could use some servants.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:41.550
"You all, come with me," The Mask ordered,
flexing its iron will and quickly capturing

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:45.560
the weak, fear-addled minds of the D-Class
personnel before it.

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:50.180
They fell in line, shuffling out the door
and following the Mask with the same blank

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:52.700
expressions as the guard before.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:57.200
Whatever was left of their personalities after
so much time being used and abused by the

00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:03.070
Foundation, it was gone now, replaced only
with the will of the mighty Mask.

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:07.950
As the Mask continued its victory tour of
the Foundation, now with four mindless servants

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:10.870
in tow, it passed the staff break room.

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:16.230
Through the window, it spotted one Dr. Bright,
the telltale amulet around his neck, microwaving

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:18.360
some leftover pizza.

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:23.430
The Mask had always found Dr. Bright distasteful,
with his self-aggrandizing pranks and general

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:26.930
dedication to chaos with no grand vision behind
it,

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:29.090
no meaningful agenda.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.660
It was pitiful.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:32.320
It was deeply ugly.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:37.410
And now, the Mask had a chance to put an end
to the immortal Doctor's antics once and for

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:38.410
all.

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:42.500
It opened the door, greeting Dr. Bright with
that frozen grin.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.290
"Oh, Doctor..."

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:49.560
Dr. Bright's eyes widened, and he didn't even
hear the microwave behind him ding, signaling

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.100
that his pizza was ready.

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:54.440
He was too distracted by the horrifying sight
before him.

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:59.070
But as he opened his mouth to scream, to quip,
to call for help, the Mask reached out and

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:01.030
ripped the amulet from his neck.

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:06.089
The host body fell limply to the ground, and
the Mask looked down at the amulet, glinting

00:17:06.089 --> 00:17:09.990
in the light, that held Dr. Bright's consciousness
inside.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:15.699
It stared at the amulet with a flinty gaze,
and under its empty stare, the metal began

00:17:15.699 --> 00:17:21.510
to rust, to degrade, and to melt into an unrecognizable
slurry.

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:26.870
The Mask let it drip onto the floor, then,
when all that was Dr. Bright had melted away,

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:32.630
it wiped its hand off with a napkin, and ground
the wet puddle on the ground with its heel.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:34.509
"Goodbye, Doctor."

00:17:34.509 --> 00:17:36.010
The Mask hissed.

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:38.590
"Now, what's next!"

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:44.710
But as the Mask turned to walk down the hall,
it came face to face with a disapproving face.

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:50.389
SCP-343 had manifested directly in front of
the Mask, and he clearly had learned of the

00:17:50.389 --> 00:17:52.990
Mask's behavior so far that day.

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:55.909
"You've been busy," 343 remarked.

00:17:55.909 --> 00:17:57.659
"Yes, very busy.

00:17:57.659 --> 00:18:02.230
Lots to do, you see," The Mask chuckled smugly.

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:07.320
"You understand why I can't allow this to
continue?"

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:09.480
343's expression remained stern but calm.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:11.650
"You believe you can stop me?"

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:14.169
The Mask tilted its head to the side.

00:18:14.169 --> 00:18:16.120
"Of course, I can."

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:17.120
SCP-343 sighed.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:22.450
"But you could stop on your own, if you would
rather.

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:25.860
I'd prefer to avoid an unnecessary conflict."

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:32.159
The Mask giggled uncontrollably at this.

00:18:32.159 --> 00:18:40.110
"I'm going to rend the flesh from your bones,"
It simply said.

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:43.710
"I thought you might say something like that.

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:47.860
I'm going to have to take your body.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:48.980
I'm sorry."

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:54.370
SCP-343 prepared to teleport the Mask's new
body to another location, separating them

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:58.280
and reducing the Mask to its original, more
manageable state.

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:04.179
But before he could, there was suddenly darkness
in the room, every light blinking out all

00:19:04.179 --> 00:19:05.190
at once.

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:10.429
The hall was plunged into shadow, but this
was no ordinary darkness.

00:19:10.429 --> 00:19:17.139
This darkness was inky, thick, choking like
smoke clinging to the inside of your throat.

00:19:17.139 --> 00:19:21.279
Then, just as suddenly as it appeared, the
darkness dissipated.

00:19:21.279 --> 00:19:24.009
But SCP-343 was gone.

00:19:24.009 --> 00:19:28.320
He hadn't teleported himself to somewhere
else, he hadn't walked through the wall to

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:30.010
get away from the Mask.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:32.409
He was truly gone.

00:19:32.409 --> 00:19:38.700
The Mask couldn't be certain exactly what
it had done to SCP-343, but it knew that the

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:40.830
enemy had been truly eradicated.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:47.080
In fact, it was fairly certain he had been
erased from reality entirely.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:52.230
The Mask made one final lap around the Foundation
Containment Site, bidding farewell to every

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.309
anomaly it passed.

00:19:54.309 --> 00:19:58.730
Some it transformed, like it had done to SCP-682.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:04.340
Taking inspiration from its bird-like face,
the Mask turned the Plague Doctor into a crow.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:11.289
Others it simply executed, such as the poor
SCP-096, whose screams and shrieks had always

00:20:11.289 --> 00:20:12.669
irritated the Mask.

00:20:12.669 --> 00:20:17.130
Of course, Foundation staff began to notice
what was happening, and they tried to defeat

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:18.130
the Mask.

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:22.970
They shot at it with their puny weapons, they
sounded their useless alarms, and they called

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:24.919
for their laughable backup.

00:20:24.919 --> 00:20:28.499
But none of it mattered, not in the face of
the Mask.

00:20:28.499 --> 00:20:33.549
Guns melted in guards' hands, alarms went
silent at nothing more than a glance, and

00:20:33.549 --> 00:20:37.380
more and more mindless slaves joined the Mask's
army.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:41.260
It didn't want too many, that would just be
difficult to keep track of.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:45.289
But an even dozen seemed like the perfect
number.

00:20:45.289 --> 00:20:50.700
With this miniature army in tow, the Mask
finally made its way to its final destination:

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:51.809
The Exit.

00:20:51.809 --> 00:20:57.520
It had been waiting for this moment, dreaming
of it, since it was first imprisoned so long

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.669
ago.

00:20:58.669 --> 00:21:03.020
As it stepped out into the sun, the Mask realized
that, though it didn't have nostrils,

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:07.830
it could smell the breeze, the scent of wildflowers
and grass.

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:13.490
What a beautiful place to mold in the Mask's
image of an ideal world.

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:18.710
The world was its oyster, and The Mask longed
to swallow it whole.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:22.070
The current whereabouts of The Possessive
Mask are unknown.

00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:24.690
The Foundation is doing its best to locate
the Mask,

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:30.629
and determine new effective measures for bringing
it down and re-containing it as soon as possible.

00:21:30.629 --> 00:21:36.390
The escape of the Mask is being considered
a possible XK-Class End of the World Scenario,if

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:38.210
it cannot be stopped.

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:41.610
The best and brightest minds at the Foundation
are working on it,

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:45.460
aside from Dr. Bright of course, may he rest
in peace.

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:48.779
But right now, there is very little anyone
can do.

00:21:48.779 --> 00:21:54.590
So, if you see a strange dark figure in a
white mask walking down your street, do yourself

00:21:54.590 --> 00:21:59.730
a favor and run the other way, before it's
too late.

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:03.990
Now go check out “Could SCP-682 be Contained
in the Backrooms?”

00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:09.739
and “SCP-096 VS Siren Head” for more terrifying
anomalous hypotheticals!

